[{"id":"VRCE-4-34-1","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":34,"verse":1,"english":"When Sumitra's son, Laksmana, had spoken thus, flaming in energy, Tārā of face fair as the moon, said to him,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-35-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4034001","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"07217d456e5878d109fdf4bb4a292cdac682830f18e212097bcf3952b1b2a072","compact":"b740ffc947bc857179cc7b6f5e4fdbac1fbbfa7b37e410b611b511fe970a207c","nasal":"b740ffc947bc857179cc7b6f5e4fdbac1fbbfa7b37e410b611b511fe970a207c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-34-2","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":34,"verse":2,"english":"O Lakşmaņa, you ought not to speak thus: and this lord of monkeys does not deserve to hear this harsh speech from your lips, in especial.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-35-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4034002","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"49527c750dc42ea706983b3a174f4e8f693319168088ce1912384d8c6a1c485e","compact":"317d516e19a4f91f76b457acbaf9c5118b1222939154116a33966ba1cf78d153","nasal":"317d516e19a4f91f76b457acbaf9c5118b1222939154116a33966ba1cf78d153"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-34-3","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":34,"verse":3,"english":"Sugrīva is not ungrateful, or cunning, or heartless; nor does he, O hero, deal in falsehood; nor is he deceitful.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-35-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4034003","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2da9270e8cf4b660d9b689777342fff1e5cb12400006be59c2248651a39a75cc","compact":"5da378ff1085efcc647d2f7b9ca3700520d326bb337fb79045b903d2946826b7","nasal":"5da378ff1085efcc647d2f7b9ca3700520d326bb337fb79045b903d2946826b7"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-34-4","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":34,"verse":4,"english":"Nor has the heroic monkey, O hero, forgotten the good, incapable of being done by others in battle, that the hero; Rāma, has done in his behalf.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-35-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4034004","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d650b51d87178b51729c609b39719224a753a540dfd25983a2746dfd270f3575","compact":"afe9622720a0aa013f0d964603d59be7fbd9d04c650e06d9e4c24d3128999c3c","nasal":"afe9622720a0aa013f0d964603d59be7fbd9d04c650e06d9e4c24d3128999c3c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-34-5","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":34,"verse":5,"english":"O afflictor of foes, through Rāma's grace, Sugriva has here attained fame and the enduring empire of the monkeys, as well as Umā and myself.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-35-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4034005","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"26d99041392f0fcb931b5bd4b2f5d168cd6da767de4dcd15343e6f6e44c7057d","compact":"ca5b84888bbfc696790dec70deb660d92b918d7fc236f3d11d42ffa28e974b67","nasal":"7b21f70623fd25d69287bc6edec3de0a179899cdf426df3bff2099288210808f"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-34-6","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":34,"verse":6,"english":"Having lain down miserable before, Sugrīva, now that he has attained this supreme happiness, does not heed his urgent duties, like the ascetic Visvamitra.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-35-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4034006","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6d40aaa0e4f309697cefae8e609993b8ec755b408c35beea7f544297c12f4e75","compact":"0e7e0baff69cb73dac84c242722f7a743220104480c3d4b712469821a0630f1a","nasal":"fe6c5f34264dca0dfebe6d81e7f0e7dd9460e4233b3975f81b94ef04c248c614"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-34-7","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":34,"verse":7,"english":"Attached to Ghrtāci, O Laksmana, the pious and mighty ascetic, Viśvāmitra looked upon ten years as one day; and that best of those conversant with time, Viśvāmitra of mighty energy, did not perceive that the time (for doing a certain act) had arrived. What is to be said of other people?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-35-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4034007","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a9c8d9960f98643c0f8568681c3845053ffc5fd9f2f9a7013aee5c9ea0049550","compact":"9cea12e16d4909005729146f76268d67e42ea932af8b0af4c364c442bd460ab6","nasal":"9cea12e16d4909005729146f76268d67e42ea932af8b0af4c364c442bd460ab6"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-34-8","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":34,"verse":8,"english":"Attached to Ghrtāci, O Laksmana, the pious and mighty ascetic, Viśvāmitra looked upon ten years as one day; and that best of those conversant with time, Viśvāmitra of mighty energy, did not perceive that the time (for doing a certain act) had arrived. What is to be said of other people?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-35-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4034008","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7bf20fdd8736c344fc5b1d75fdbdc7d602294afc80a89ecd6064742afe3f434a","compact":"4c56142a2ac297570ad989a91ed57bd3ec19968ed72ccdd3af5d1625ec5e98ba","nasal":"4c56142a2ac297570ad989a91ed57bd3ec19968ed72ccdd3af5d1625ec5e98ba"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-34-9","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":34,"verse":9,"english":"O Lakşmaņa, it behoveth Rāma to forgive one who has all the bodily exigencies, who is fatigued, and who is not satisfied with the pleasures of Kama. Nor, O Laksmana, does it behove you, without ascertaining the exact import of things, to become suddenly subject to wrath, like any inferior person.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.881,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-35-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4034009","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ca2ef9ee4f327dd93f482cfb1c7baaa3c6839829b88052aa87ae68497a74126b","compact":"1a573605dd16ab44b05f5432d9ae277358efedd9d5f3e5baf85cab2c9d0b1ada","nasal":"c6f9a0ff32e6aa9fc82ff9a4bf650226731dd8bf2203e2f72a1873e204cbe515"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-34-10","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":34,"verse":10,"english":"O Lakşmaņa, it behoveth Rāma to forgive one who has all the bodily exigencies, who is fatigued, and who is not satisfied with the pleasures of Kama. Nor, O Laksmana, does it behove you, without ascertaining the exact import of things, to become suddenly subject to wrath, like any inferior person.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-35-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4034010","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fe09e1b73f7abafd0b248f0cc00ca413a7092799f089c6f8809887712748eb95","compact":"80814f13d9ae87693576c136f6086eb760e9516d06d96b8ef61be34f1a422629","nasal":"9e273d28084f1234aaf9b0cfdb1c3b9dd36eb219d890b27f02cc769edad621fe"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-34-11","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":34,"verse":11,"english":"O chief of men, persons endowed with the quality of goodness, like to you, do not suffer themselves to come under the sway of passion, without (at first) heedfully revolving matters.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.881,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-35-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4034011","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f0d11ffb8d1a4b5530509372b9118386109e25df23812995c54f7056a410fbfa","compact":"f831838a0e90d85927a21369248d25585609bd3091475544c015633b9b6e7574","nasal":"9420bb20f1dba6f9f4d83fdc5c8c7428d1d428fa3582c80a00008bc228eb7dd3"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-34-12","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":34,"verse":12,"english":"I crave your favour with concentrated mind, O you that know morality. Renounce the mighty grief that springs from your ire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.886,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-35-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4034012","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3f7098bedf47cd0b79bc1a9f097508503018501642b4223cd0e131ffd4fff34c","compact":"dbc988936b98f3bd72e974a6c48c8bd42177e1f5de4c2c9f487e1c6cd4e1b6d1","nasal":"c18480df833f1f2f50cd90ad5d5b127cb789b78589c84bc18e260cf54d8aaa14"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-34-13","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":34,"verse":13,"english":"This is my conviction that for compassing Rāma's welfare, Sugrīva can resign Umã and myself, and Angada, and the kingdom and wealth and corn and animals.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.581,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-35-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4034013","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b33c60dfe1e9df2443d2d8a94a1d1b29727baeaec25d4a8fd645196537a9cac8","compact":"44361ceaac31cca49ce8d32c61039e13f25631608194d6fa572ade199ffbf1e3","nasal":"44361ceaac31cca49ce8d32c61039e13f25631608194d6fa572ade199ffbf1e3"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-34-14","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":34,"verse":14,"english":"Slaying that worst of Rākṣasas, Sugrīva will bring Rāghava with Sītā, like to the moon accompanied by Rohiņi.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.534,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-35-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4034014","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a029d2bf0028a8dd05586539500f62b3169acca3a37626f7dbc82e44e8b3ef6e","compact":"39d0e7464ec2d8ebcbd81c96ac95c0daa39785b4fc9431a76c349d439b46588f","nasal":"e3267b01eb223137348088f455e0ad773eee7f5b6011611c53ecab5bb1af6b5c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-34-15","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":34,"verse":15,"english":"Without slaying hundreds of thousands of Kotis, and thirty-six Ayutas, thousands and hundreds of irrepressible Rākṣasas wearing shapes at will, (Rāma) can not slay Rāvana, by whom Maithili has been carried away.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-35-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4034015","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b11dfbf69395cb072199c34aa50f366d7cfdef77f35aa751da2792004ef509cf","compact":"b070ea01a088b500bcc89303ba644b27fb440f0b2fed129182e3fce3ae333ba9","nasal":"4d5f008ba419ec015c2959ee9b5cf85c58104ccdb262237bdd660f0b5b8eef1e"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-34-16","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":34,"verse":16,"english":"Without slaying hundreds of thousands of Kotis, and thirty-six Ayutas, thousands and hundreds of irrepressible Rākṣasas wearing shapes at will, (Rāma) can not slay Rāvana, by whom Maithili has been carried away.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-35-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4034016","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"02c6ae2736b80d17089fbfa0471fefe5753a69b11fbc31ef76952c14ce8febb7","compact":"ec59e3e2c8ad7143368c035a236c92cb359be1a7c045f0e9bc7e9575e8872524","nasal":"ab803afac3640e70c83d2f97564abe8b7adc3063fd8ad3383141e9556f547b65"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-34-17","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":34,"verse":17,"english":"They are incapable, O Laksmana, of being slain (by Rāma) in battle, unless he is supported (by others).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-35-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4034017","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4d8f2ed11144b3f8dee4c3cf7c115f0df9fafbf531bf2411c665e28bd2ea6c3e","compact":"387f4f38d87ed651e8b687f718c4c7855f7d346660559977dd9c8aee01efae99","nasal":"9ff2c3e8cad41ca206345403c993418b185179369e7853439cadd7956ef013fb"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-34-18","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":34,"verse":18,"english":"Rāvana is a wily warrior, and hence is the special need of Sugrīva. That knowing lord of monkeys, Väli, had told me all this. I do not know how Rāvana had secured this host: I say what I had heard from Vāli.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-35-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4034018","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7b1e0123d897ba21df57b73adc7f149eae4757c2b50bbd598a0d006979452841","compact":"95f4dccc58720daf01a6fc745bf8cd8463bc98c42a222ffc8b825752c35cf3a7","nasal":"95f4dccc58720daf01a6fc745bf8cd8463bc98c42a222ffc8b825752c35cf3a7"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-34-19","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":34,"verse":19,"english":"For rendering you assistance, the foremost monkeys have been despatched in order to summon to the conflict numerous principal monkeys.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.636,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-35-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4034019","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b910236f512c396d899b34aad770546f4cfd989984580e86ce96fdce032e05a1","compact":"49ac1ada7e64690c0a9deef6c7114c83a383373df8af774f9d69bc5f57d3729e","nasal":"49ac1ada7e64690c0a9deef6c7114c83a383373df8af774f9d69bc5f57d3729e"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-34-20","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":34,"verse":20,"english":"Expecting these powerful and exceedingly strong ones, for attaining Rāghava's end, this lord of monkeys does not (yet) sally out.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-35-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4034020","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f73cb39eccc92c8d291cba52c58d4dd8a617f26aaf7c4f184827030237bd52c5","compact":"3025c7d7e7a79d2d3bd6f62450a7b3e90246b302459bb9d97c32dba3e6f9b8f4","nasal":"94ba74e6cb5d90833b9f06fa2dcbc2383a71d02b03ed9b619dafd2172bc637b5"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-34-21","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":34,"verse":21,"english":"Things, O Saumitri, have beforehand been so satisfactorily arranged by Sugrīva, that this very day the mighty one will be joined with all those monkeys.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.591,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-35-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4034021","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"900e8396d731990a97e427751ac85631dda8b144685709a9118fcd9134e1234c","compact":"16cff2ee28ecee774de236a136375be2a60ffce90ace8f4bc44ffd599239f161","nasal":"9e747333ff16dd2f8a2b23923c46dc99482a217a5c9c514bfe81a7eebd3c40ec"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-34-22","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":34,"verse":22,"english":"This very day billions of bears and thousands of golangulas as well as innumerable Koțis of monkeys flaming in energy shall join you. Therefore, O subduer of enemies, banish your anger.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.763,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-35-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4034022","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"155159ebc285bec6e6a7ef9f0d87f60d49a093215b15d147bccf5fbd318a4810","compact":"2feac31ee20c42607db55ae4fd79c27316ebbcab1939e1c6bbf67e2ded34297f","nasal":"8e3b5dfeca56f86e5dc5554e92aec349b6cc2944bff219cffaa660f0ef58d966"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-34-23","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":34,"verse":23,"english":"Seeing this your face wrought up with wrath, and your eyes appearing like red sores, the wives of the best of monkeys experience no peace, and they are agitated by the fear that exercised them of late.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.814,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-35-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4034023","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e769a0779a7f42e9360f5abbb4e3969fea6d3b611a1c06ed49e09f943cef9b58","compact":"84c03afecd9a446197f97b0a2c239f9db0666f42d97ace5e40b5f71216d439cc","nasal":"4ffb0c0eadbebf64e26ff3f9fb835eebdcf04ad79ee64f39ef8da949e3c69f0e"}}]
